From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Baron <dbaron@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 16:47:07 -0700
Subject: Ensure sufficient lifetime of WebViewImpl::page_popup_.

This is a straightforward fix that I think should be suitable for
backporting to branches.  In the longer term we might want to make
WebPagePopupImpl garbage collected, but that's a bit more involved.

I verified that the added unittest (built by Gemini from the original
testcase) does exercise the need for both the scoped_refptr in
WebViewImpl::UpdatePagePopup and the null-check in
WebPagePopupImpl::Update, both of which are also needed to fix the
original testcase.

Fixed: 565774991
Change-Id: I828fe321e04a74bf9f6ba25222c507197082cbc3
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8464185
Commit-Queue: David Baron <dbaron@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Joey Arhar <jarhar@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1705319}

Electron adaptation notes (42-x-y): brace style of the surrounding single-line
if statements in web_view_impl.cc / web_page_popup_impl.cc differs on this
branch (context only). Test-only hunks in internal_popup_menu_test.cc
conflicted with unrelated test drift and were dropped.

